  "body": "Found in the #3743 research. Part of #3743 (out of its 2D scope, tracked here so that it is not lost).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe 3D ladder has its own copies of the 2D link and entry code, with the same names:\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/descent.rs:264` (`descend`) and `crates/motion/src/machining2d/ladder_links.rs:58` (`descend`).\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/level_ctx.rs:198` (`dive_link`) and `crates/motion/src/machining2d/descent_dive.rs:45` (`dive_link`).\n- `crates/motion/src/machining3d/hsm.rs:296` (`microlift`) and `crates/motion/src/machining2d/microlift.rs:104` (`link`).\n\nUsers: 3D Pocket, Rotary Offset, Multi-axis rough.\n\n## Wanted\n\nAfter step 1 of #3743 (#3750), compare each pair. Where the law is the same, make the 3D code call `ring_links` and `ring_entry`. Where it differs, write why in a comment at the 3D function.\n\n## Pins (equivalence)\n\n- The CL moves of `crates/motion/tests/pocket3d_pass_start.rs` and `crates/motion/tests/level_links.rs` (3D ladder cases) are the same as on the head before the change.\n\nEffort `high`: link and entry code under the safety floor. Priority P7: a follow-up found during research, with no defect.\n\nDone means: each pair is merged or has a comment that says why it differs.\n",
